// Nothing to release. GuiDesignerTab is a real dockable tab now, but it
// registers its own ClosingOperation with ClosingOperationsManager and adds
// itself as a dependency of the root window, so the docking framework closes
// it with everything else -- there is no separate teardown for this file to
// call. Compare modules/scinotes/etc/scinotes.quit, which DOES need one:
// closeEditor() exists because SciNotes keeps editor state of its own that
// outlives the tab. The designer keeps none: the Design is read-only, the
// file on disk is already whatever the last save left, and phase 1 has no
// unsaved state to prompt about.
//
// Revisit in phase 2, when editing means there IS unsaved state -- that is
// where askForClosing() stops returning null.
